### Pro Tip for your Software Engineering class

In the HTML above, you can see `
<tr>
    ` (table row) repeated 6 times. This is "Hard Coding" and is bad practice in software engineering because if the price changes, you have to edit the HTML file.

    In a real C# ASP.NET Core application, you would create a **ViewModel** and pass a list of cars to the View.

    [Image of ASP.NET Core MVC Model View Controller data flow]

    Your view would then look like this, which is much cleaner:
@* 
    ```cshtml
@model IEnumerable<CarViewModel>

    <tbody>
        @foreach (var car in Model)
        {
            <tr>
                <td class="car-image"><div class="img" style="background-image:url('@car.ImageUrl');"></div></td>
                <td class="product-name"><h3>@car.Name</h3>...</td>
                <!-- etc -->
            </tr>
        }
    </tbody> *@
